The ISiloBuilder and IClientBuilder interfaces are not found in the expected paths. Since the class CosmosClusteringProviderBuilder is internal and the builder interfaces are not accessible or found, I cannot directly test the Configure methods by calling them with mocks.

Instead, I will write tests that mock IConfigurationSection and IServiceProvider and verify that when the Configure method is called on CosmosClusteringProviderBuilder, the GetConnectionString extension method is called on the root IConfiguration. To do this, I will create a test class in the same namespace Orleans.Hosting and make the test class a friend assembly if needed. I will also create minimal mocks for the builder interfaces to call Configure.

I will submit a test file with these tests now. It will focus on verifying the call to GetConnectionString on the root IConfiguration when ConnectionName is provided and ConnectionString is empty.

