The class CosmosClusteringProviderBuilder is internal and not accessible from the test project, and the refactor tool is not available to add test seams. Also, the builder interfaces require many members to be implemented for mocking, making direct testing difficult.

Given these constraints, the best approach is to write tests that mock IConfigurationSection and IServiceProvider and verify the behavior of the Configure method indirectly by creating minimal test doubles for the builder interfaces and options interfaces. I will make the UsedConnectionString property public set so I can assert on it.

I will submit a revised test file with these changes now. It will test that when ConnectionName is provided and ConnectionString is empty, the GetConnectionString extension method is called and the connection string is passed to ConfigureCosmosClient. The test doubles will implement the required members minimally.

